---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const posts = (await getCollection('blog')).sort(
  (a, b) => b.data.publishDate.valueOf() - a.data.publishDate.valueOf()
);

const title = 'B2B Sourcing Blog — Importing from Iran | Palude';
const description =
  'Practical guides for international B2B buyers importing from Iran: saffron sourcing, pistachio wholesale, Persian carpet authentication, export documentation, cold-chain logistics, payment methods and market trends.';

const blogSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Blog',
  name: 'Palude B2B Sourcing Blog',
  url: 'https://palude.ir/blog/',
  description,
  blogPost: posts.map((p) => ({
    '@type': 'BlogPosting',
    headline: p.data.h1,
    url: `https://palude.ir/blog/${p.slug}/`,
    datePublished: p.data.publishDate.toISOString(),
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Palude' },
  })),
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} jsonLd={blogSchema}>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Blog', href: '/blog/' }]} />

  <section class="container-wide py-14 sm:py-20">
    <header class="max-w-2xl">
      <p class="mb-3 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">B2B sourcing knowledge</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-extrabold leading-tight text-foreground text-balance sm:text-5xl">
        Practical guides for importing from Iran
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground/80 text-pretty">
        Field-tested sourcing guides, quality standards, logistics routes, payment methods and
        documentation checklists for international B2B buyers. Written by the Palude export desk
        for buyers who need to make decisions, not read marketing.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1.4fr_1fr] lg:items-start">
      <article class="prose-palude max-w-none">
        <h2>What this blog covers</h2>
        <p>
          The Palude B2B sourcing blog is the working library we wish every international buyer had
          before their first Iranian import contract. Each post is written by the export desk that
          ships the cargo, not by a marketing team, and each post answers a specific question a real
          buyer has asked us during a sourcing engagement. The categories below map to the decisions
          a buyer makes in sequence: which grade to specify, how to verify quality, how to route the
          payment, how to package and ship, and how to read the market the cargo is being bought into.
        </p>
        <p>
          The sourcing guides walk through a complete import sequence end to end, from the first
          inquiry to the delivered container. The quality and standards guides cover the lab
          frameworks, grading systems and authentication disciplines that separate a verified
          shipment from a misrepresented one. The logistics and packaging guides cover the reefer,
          dry-container and crating decisions that determine whether the product arrives as the
          product the buyer ordered. The finance guides cover the sanctions-compliant payment
          channels that actually work for Iranian exports. And the market-trends posts cover the
          harvest cycles, capacity additions and demand patterns that shape pricing across the year.
        </p>
        <p>
          We publish new guides as the trade environment shifts — when a destination authority
          tightens an aflatoxin limit, when a payment corridor opens or closes, when a harvest
          volume comes in above or below expectation. If you are building an annual sourcing
          programme, the market-trends posts are the ones to read first; if you are placing your
          first order, start with the documentation checklist and the vertical-specific guide for
          the product you are buying.
        </p>

        <h2>How to use these guides</h2>
        <p>
          Each guide is self-contained but cross-references the others where the workflow connects.
          A buyer importing <a href="/blog/how-to-import-iranian-saffron-b2b-guide/">Iranian saffron into the EU</a>
          will be directed to the <a href="/blog/iran-export-documentation-checklist/">documentation checklist</a>
          for the payment and customs workflow, and to the <a href="/blog/packaging-standards-iranian-food-exports/">packaging standards guide</a>
          for the argon-flushed foil-pouch spec that protects ISO 3632 values in transit. A buyer
          importing <a href="/export/persian-rug-9x12-hand-knotted/">hand-knotted 9x12 Persian rugs</a> will be
          directed to the <a href="/blog/persian-carpet-authentication-verify-hand-knotted/">authentication guide</a>
          for the knot-density, dye-analysis and age-verification framework. The cross-references
          exist because no single guide covers the full import workflow — the workflow is a chain,
          and each guide covers one link.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you have a question that is not covered here, the fastest path to an answer is a direct
          inquiry. We respond within one business day, and questions that recur across buyers become
          the next posts on this blog. <a href="/contact/">Request a sourcing quote</a> and an advisor
          will pick up the file.
        </p>

        <h2>Who writes these guides</h2>
        <p>
          The guides are written by the Palude export desk — the same team that issues proforma
          invoices, supervises loading at the Iranian packing facility, and resolves the
          documentation discrepancies that surface at destination customs. The perspective is the
          operator's perspective, not the consultant's: every recommendation in these guides is one
          we have implemented on a real shipment, and every warning is a failure mode we have seen
          on a real shipment that did not go to plan.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not write generic import-export content. If a guide exists on this blog, it exists
          because a buyer asked us the question and the answer was not obvious — and because the
          same question has recurred across enough buyers that publishing the answer is more
          efficient than answering it one email at a time. The guides are opinionated where the
          trade has opinions (Sargol versus Super Negin for industrial buyers; drum versus Iso-tank
          for bitumen; third-country correspondent versus letter of credit for first-time payments)
          and neutral where the trade is genuinely product- and destination-specific.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are a journalist or researcher writing about the Iranian export trade and would
          like source material, we are happy to share the underlying data behind the market-trends
          posts. Reach out through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> and we will route the
          inquiry to the desk lead for the relevant vertical.
        </p>
      </article>

      <aside class="rounded-2xl border border-border bg-secondary/50 p-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-lg font-bold text-foreground">Most-read guides</h2>
        <ol class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
          <li><a href="/blog/how-to-import-iranian-saffron-b2b-guide/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">How to import Iranian saffron: a B2B guide</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/iran-export-documentation-checklist/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Iran export documentation checklist</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/payment-methods-iranian-exports-b2b/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Payment methods for Iranian exports</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/shipping-dates-from-iran-cold-chain/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Shipping dates from Iran: cold-chain logistics</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/iranian-pistachio-quality-standards-aflatoxin/" class="font-medium text-primary hover:underline">Iranian pistachio quality standards</a></li>
        </ol>
      </aside>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-16 font-display text-2xl font-bold text-foreground">All guides</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-7 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {posts.map((post) => (
        <article class="group flex flex-col overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border bg-background shadow-sm transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lg">
          <a href={`/blog/${post.slug}/`} class="block">
            <div class="h-48 overflow-hidden">
              <img
                src={post.data.heroImage}
                alt={post.data.heroAlt}
                class="h-full w-full object-cover transition-transform duration-500 group-hover:scale-105"
                loading="lazy"
                width="940"
                height="650"
              />
            </div>
          </a>
          <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col p-5">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">{post.data.category}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-lg font-bold leading-snug text-foreground">
              <a href={`/blog/${post.slug}/`} class="transition-colors hover:text-primary">
                {post.data.h1}
              </a>
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-2 flex-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground/70">{post.data.description}</p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-muted-foreground">
              <time datetime={post.data.publishDate.toISOString()}>
                {post.data.publishDate.toLocaleDateString('en-US', { year: 'numeric', month: 'short', day: 'numeric' })}
              </time>
              <span>{post.data.readingTime}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
